hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1387","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha said: The sun eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he went out to the mosque, stood up and said the takbir and lined up the people behind him. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited a long recitation, then he said “Allahu Akbar,” and bowed for a long time, then raised his head and said: “God has heard whoever Praise Him, “Our Lord, and to You be all praise.” Then he got up and recited a long recitation, which was closer than the first recitation. Then he said “Allah is Great” and bowed for a long time, which was closer than the first recitation. The first bowing, then he said: “God hears whoever praises Him. Our Lord, and praise be to You.” Then he did the same in the last rak’ah, completing four rak’ahs. He performed four prostrations, and the sun set before he left. Then he got up and addressed the people, praising God as He deserved it, then he said: “Indeed The sun and the moon are two signs of God that will not be eclipsed by anyone’s death or his life, so when you see them, prepare for prayer.”"
